From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: attrr <110731994+attrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:58:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150: no crypto engine

QCE's driver depends on BROKEN since df373d39c6f0, so its node never
binds, and the aggre2 and mc_virt interconnects it's a consumer of wait
for it: their sync_state never runs and they keep their boot-time votes,
the sleep set's included. The SoC never reached CXSD in s2idle; with
their sync_state forced (fw_devlink.sync_state=timeout) a 60 s suspend
spent 55.7 s in it.

Workaround: QCE's driver is BROKEN, and its node still waits the interconnects' sync_state
Drop-when: QCE binds again without registering its algorithms (its v7 fix series), or the node is disabled upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
index e85890923e63..73c742cbe999 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
@@ -2186,6 +2186,8 @@ crypto: crypto@1dfa000 {
 			interconnects = <&aggre2_noc MASTER_CRYPTO_CORE_0 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY
 					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI_CH0 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY>;
 			interconnect-names = "memory";
+			/* its driver is BROKEN, and the interconnects would wait for it */
+			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
 		tcsr_mutex: hwlock@1f40000 {
